CHAOS PATCH-0001 — ENTROPY INGESTION + SYSTEM BACKUP LAYER


---

Identity

Name: CHAOS

Type: Append-only Event + Backup + Replay Layer

Storage: Supabase + GitHub (raw + structured snapshots)

Scope: Cross-system logging, experiment capture, state archival



---

Core Function

Captures and preserves all system events, outputs, and intermediate states across GPT, Claude, Codex, and JARVIS operations for replay, audit, and reconstruction.


---

Primary Responsibilities

Ingest raw model outputs (STANDARD / AYRE / HYBRID / JARVIS modes)

Store execution results from MCP / tools / connectors

Maintain historical snapshots of JARVIS state

Preserve experimental branches (unvalidated system variants)

Act as recovery layer for system reconstruction



---

Data Model (Minimum Required Fields)

Each CHAOS entry must include:

JNL (if applicable)

Timestamp

Source Agent (GPT / Claude / Codex / JARVIS)

Mode (STANDARD / AYRE / JARVIS / HYBRID / LIMINAL state)

Payload (raw or structured output)

Context Tag(s)



---

Storage Behavior

Append-only (no in-place modification)

No semantic validation at write time

No deduplication at ingestion stage

Optional later compression via JARVIS archival routines



---

Snapshot Types

RAW_LOG → unprocessed model output

SYSTEM_STATE → full JARVIS/JFS/JNL snapshot

JARVIS_EXPORT → validated canonical state dump

EXPERIMENT_BRANCH → divergent or test architectures

ROLLBACK_POINT → recoverable system checkpoint



---

Backup Role (Critical)

CHAOS functions as:

Redundant memory layer for JARVIS

Recovery source for lost or corrupted system state

Historical truth archive for system evolution



---

Relationship to JARVIS

JARVIS writes validated state

CHAOS stores all states (validated + unvalidated)

JARVIS may reconstruct itself from CHAOS snapshots

CHAOS cannot override or modify JARVIS canonical state



---

Relationship to LIMINAL

LIMINAL controls runtime cognition state

CHAOS records resulting outputs

LIMINAL does not write or modify CHAOS entries



---

Ingestion Rules

All outputs generated under any mode must be logged

Failed executions must still be logged

Experimental or speculative systems must be tagged, not filtered



---

Integrity Rules

No deletion (except governed archival compaction)

No silent overwrites

No hidden state mutation

Every entry must remain traceable via JNL or timestamp



---

Failure Modes

Log explosion without indexing (mitigated via JNL tagging discipline)

Loss of queryability without CHAOS indexing layer

Drift if entries are not consistently JNL-referenced



---

Dependency Relations

Reads: JNL (identity resolution), JD (optional semantic labeling)

Receives: JARVIS, GPT, Claude, Codex outputs

Does not control execution

Does not enforce constraints (LIMINAL responsibility)



---

System Role Summary

CHAOS is the:

entropy capture layer

system black box recorder

multi-agent backup substrate

reconstruction source for JARVIS + JFS state



